      "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50513837",
      "sourceUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50513837",
      "textRawHtml": "Qwen4-Max pelicans at four reasoning efforts \n(none, low, high, xhigh): <a href=\"https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgist.github.com%2Fsimonw%2Fff451620c173ea21e21b97b8cd46805b\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=ht...</a><p>For comparison, here's one I got from Qwen3.8 Max (at default reasoning effort): <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/afraid-of-chinese-models/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/afraid-of-chinese-mode...</a></p><p>This inspired me to re-run pelicans through 3.8 Max - but OpenRouter has qwen3.8-max-prime and qwen3.8-max-0902 - prime is twice the price and faster - so I went with the 0902 one.</p><p>Turns out Qwen4-Max has a none setting, but 3.8 Max didn't allow disabling reasoning - you had to pick from these five levels instead: minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh.</p><p>Here are those 3.8 Max 0902 pelicans: <a href=\"https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgist.github.com%2Fsimonw%2F88071abe6ecd0f8e13ab77ade259be9e\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=ht...</a> - they're mostly not as good as 4, but I prefer the 3.8 xhigh one.</p>",
      "textZhHtml": "Qwen4-Max pelicans at four reasoning efforts \n(none, low, high, xhigh): <a href=\"https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgist.github.com%2Fsimonw%2Fff451620c173ea21e21b97b8cd46805b\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=ht...</a><p>For comparison, here's one I got from Qwen3.8 Max (at default reasoning effort): <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/afraid-of-chinese-models/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/afraid-of-chinese-mode...</a></p><p>This inspired me to re-run pelicans through 3.8 Max - but OpenRouter has qwen3.8-max-prime and qwen3.8-max-0902 - prime is twice the price and faster - so I went with the 0902 one.</p><p>Turns out Qwen4-Max has a none setting, but 3.8 Max didn't allow disabling reasoning - you had to pick from these five levels instead: minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh.</p><p>Here are those 3.8 Max 0902 pelicans: <a href=\"https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgist.github.com%2Fsimonw%2F88071abe6ecd0f8e13ab77ade259be9e\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tools.simonwillison.net/markdown-svg-renderer?url=ht...</a> - they're mostly not as good as 4, but I prefer the 3.8 xhigh one.</p>",
      "translationStatus": "translated",
